{:edb/db-before-t 1816 :edb/db-after-t 1817 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535129 50 #inst "2026-10-08T17:36:26.858Z" 13194139535129 true] [17592186064171 1020 #edb/ref 17592186332676 13194139535129 true] [17592186068727 1020 #edb/ref 17592186332692 13194139535129 true] [17592186068848 1020 #edb/ref 17592186332684 13194139535129 true] [17592186096541 1020 #edb/ref 17592186332673 13194139535129 true] [17592186096603 1020 #edb/ref 17592186332679 13194139535129 true] [17592186096736 1020 #edb/ref 17592186332687 13194139535129 true] [17592186332673 1017 #edb/ref 17592186332674 13194139535129 true] [17592186332673 1089 "q-128235" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332673 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535129 true] [17592186332673 1100 "Consider the family of functions $f(x)=\\frac{x-2}{{x}^{2}+4x+k},$ where $k$ is a constant.\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x).$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${f}^{′}(x)\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332673 1113 #uuid "151e4a89-5fc4-53b1-88f1-d33b9974e06c" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332673 1145 "The numerator and denominator are $u(x)=x-2$ and $v(x)={x}^{2}+4x+k,$ respectively. Their derivatives are given by\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(x) & =1, \\\\ {v}^{′}(x) & =2x+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(1)({x}^{2}+4x+k)-(x-2)(2x+4)}{{({x}^{2}+4x+k)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2}+4x+k)-(2{x}^{2}-8)}{{({x}^{2}+4x+k)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-{x}^{2}+4x+k+8}{{({x}^{2}+4x+k)}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332674 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332675 13194139535129 true] [17592186332674 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535129 true] [17592186332674 1041 "field-1" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332674 1104 #edb/ref 17592186332675 13194139535129 true] [17592186332674 1110 #uuid "ab987a40-01e8-57be-89d4-b6a10d98efb0" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332675 1034 "\\frac{-x^2+4x+k+8}{(x^2+4x+k)^2}" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332675 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535129 true] [17592186332675 1111 #uuid "a9c1506f-3d2b-5086-9cc5-0bf8a0a91daf" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332676 1017 #edb/ref 17592186332677 13194139535129 true] [17592186332676 1089 "q-128236" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332676 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535129 true] [17592186332676 1100 "Consider the family of functions $f(x)=\\frac{x-2}{{x}^{2}+4x+k},$ where $k$ is a constant.\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x).$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${f}^{′}(x)\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{-x^2+4x+k+8}{(x^2+4x+k)^2}$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind the value of $k$ such that the slope of the tangent line to the curve $y=f(x)$ at the point where $x=0$ is equal to $0.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $k\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332676 1113 #uuid "f8fdffc7-7367-5862-96dc-00bc09beecc9" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332676 1145 "Previously, we found that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{-{x}^{2}+4x+k+8}{{({x}^{2}+4x+k)}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & =\\frac{-{0}^{2}+4\\cdot 0+k+8}{{({0}^{2}+4\\cdot 0+k)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{k+8}{{k}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent to the curve when $x=0$ equals $\\frac{k+8}{{k}^{2}}.$\n\nFinally, using the fact that  the slope must be equal to $0,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k+8}{{k}^{2}} & =0 \\\\ k+8 & =0 \\\\ k & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=-8.$" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332677 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332678 13194139535129 true] [17592186332677 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535129 true] [17592186332677 1041 "field-1" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332677 1104 #edb/ref 17592186332678 13194139535129 true] [17592186332677 1110 #uuid "4ad03919-68c7-5c5e-892a-4925bb97abf9" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332678 1034 "-8" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332678 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535129 true] [17592186332678 1111 #uuid "6d292964-d76c-5937-9c06-ab5f12388c27" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332679 1017 #edb/ref 17592186332680 13194139535129 true] [17592186332679 1017 #edb/ref 17592186332682 13194139535129 true] [17592186332679 1089 "q-128237" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332679 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535129 true] [17592186332679 1100 "Consider the family of functions $f(x)=\\frac{x-2}{{x}^{2}+4x+k},$ where $k$ is a constant.\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x).$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${f}^{′}(x)\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{-x^2+4x+k+8}{(x^2+4x+k)^2}$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nFind the value of $k$ such that the slope of the tangent line to the curve $y=f(x)$ at the point where $x=0$ is equal to $0.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $k\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-8$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nWhen $k=3,$ the function $f(x)$ can be written as\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{A}{x+3}+\\frac{B}{x+1},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are real constants. What are the values of $A$ and $B?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $A\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \n$\\,B\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332679 1113 #uuid "8c083f60-561a-557c-a89b-f8cab51dfc55" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332679 1145 "When $k=3,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{x-2}{{x}^{2}+4x+3}=\\frac{x-2}{(x+3)(x+1)}.\n$$\n\nOur task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-2}{(x+3)(x+1)}=\\frac{A}{x+3}+\\frac{B}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above expression through by $(x+3)(x+1)$ gives\n\n$$\nx-2=A(x+1)+B(x+3).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-3$ gets rid of the $B$ term and allows us to solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3-2 & =A(-3+1)+B(-3+3) \\\\ -5 & =-2A \\\\ A & =\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-1$ gets rid of the $A$ term and allows us to solve for $B:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1-2 & =A(-1+1)+B(-1+3) \\\\ -3 & =2B \\\\ B & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{x-2}{(x+3)(x+1)}=\\frac{5}{2(x+3)}-\\frac{3}{2(x+1)}.\n$$" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332680 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332681 13194139535129 true] [17592186332680 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535129 true] [17592186332680 1041 "field-1" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332680 1104 #edb/ref 17592186332681 13194139535129 true] [17592186332680 1110 #uuid "18188044-1dae-5eb2-9801-6f0392d2555e" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332681 1034 "\\frac{5}{2}" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332681 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535129 true] [17592186332681 1111 #uuid "667b508a-1bc5-5303-954e-060eafbeb702" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332682 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332683 13194139535129 true] [17592186332682 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535129 true] [17592186332682 1041 "field-2" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332682 1104 #edb/ref 17592186332683 13194139535129 true] [17592186332682 1110 #uuid "41516b58-7339-5281-8a5b-d6479f6d95e5" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332683 1034 "-\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332683 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535129 true] [17592186332683 1111 #uuid "d3257929-b647-5bfe-b332-b34177b5b5e7" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332684 1017 #edb/ref 17592186332685 13194139535129 true] [17592186332684 1089 "q-128238" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332684 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535129 true] [17592186332684 1100 "Consider the family of functions $f(x)=\\frac{x-2}{{x}^{2}+4x+k},$ where $k$ is a constant.\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x).$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${f}^{′}(x)\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{-x^2+4x+k+8}{(x^2+4x+k)^2}$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nFind the value of $k$ such that the slope of the tangent line to the curve $y=f(x)$ at the point where $x=0$ is equal to $0.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $k\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-8$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nWhen $k=3,$ the function $f(x)$ can be written as\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{A}{x+3}+\\frac{B}{x+1},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are real constants. What are the values of $A$ and $B?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $A\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{5}{2}$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \n$\\,B\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-\\frac{3}{2}$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind the value of ${\\int }_{-5}^{-4}\\frac{x-2}{(x+3)(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${\\int }_{-5}^{-4}\\frac{x-2}{(x+3)(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332684 1113 #uuid "09a5374f-7fae-5833-afc2-59d1e0fd4da4" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332684 1145 "Previously, we found that \n\n$$\n\\frac{x-2}{(x+3)(x+1)}=\\frac{5}{2(x+3)}-\\frac{3}{2(x+1)}.\n$$\n\nNow, we can integrate, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-2}{(x+3)(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{5}{2(x+3)}-\\frac{3}{2(x+1)})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x-\\frac{3}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the result using the laws of logarithms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C & =\\frac{1}{2}(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3{|}^{5}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1{|}^{3})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{(x+3)^{5}}{(x+1)^{3}}|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the definite integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-5}^{-4}\\frac{x-2}{(x+3)(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{(x+3)^{5}}{(x+1)^{3}}|]}_{-5}^{-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{{3}^{3}})-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{2}^{5}}{{4}^{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{4}^{3}}{{2}^{5}\\cdot {3}^{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2}{27}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332685 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332686 13194139535129 true] [17592186332685 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535129 true] [17592186332685 1041 "field-1" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332685 1104 #edb/ref 17592186332686 13194139535129 true] [17592186332685 1110 #uuid "c2038167-f157-5685-90d9-885146ed0bd0" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332686 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}\\ln(2)-\\frac{3}{2}\\ln(3)" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332686 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535129 true] [17592186332686 1111 #uuid "1a00a065-9fb2-5226-a9de-a670ae83b655" 13194139535129 true]