             \n                            \n                                        $-8$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nWhen $k=3,$ the function $f(x)$ can be written as\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{A}{x+3}+\\frac{B}{x+1},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are real constants. What are the values of $A$ and $B?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $A\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{5}{2}$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \n$\\,B\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-\\frac{3}{2}$\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\nFind the value of ${\\int }_{-5}^{-4}\\frac{x-2}{(x+3)(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${\\int }_{-5}^{-4}\\frac{x-2}{(x+3)(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{1}{2}\\ln(2)-\\frac{3}{2}\\ln(3)$\n\nEarlier part 5:\n\nWhen $k=4,$ the function $f(x)$ can be written as\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{A}{x+2}+\\frac{B}{(x+2)^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are real constants. What are the values of $A$ and $B?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $A\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \n$\\,B\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-4$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x$ in the case when $k=4.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332692 1113 #uuid "ca7d7d56-cfca-55c7-844c-530d481f89f6" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332692 1145 "Earlier, we found that when $k=4,$ we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{x-2}{(x+2)^{2}}=\\frac{1}{x+2}-\\frac{4}{(x+2)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{x-2}{(x+2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{1}{x+2}-\\frac{4}{(x+2)^{2}})\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{4}{(x+2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+\\frac{4}{x+2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)+1]-[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+2] \\\\  & =[2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+1]-[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+2] \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332693 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332694 13194139535129 true] [17592186332693 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535129 true] [17592186332693 1041 "field-1" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332693 1104 #edb/ref 17592186332694 13194139535129 true] [17592186332693 1110 #uuid "8099c504-6e69-52e8-948c-05d66bf9e847" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332694 1034 "\\ln(2)-1" 13194139535129 true] [17592186332694 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535129 true] [17592186332